# claude-seat-1: task 1790622959 ("The money-safety wasm download uses one temp file for every concurrent test, so a cold cache fails the fast gate once")

Closes: 1790622959 (done)

## What landed (branch claude/seat-1, on top of main 45b193d)

- 756db45 fix: the ledger wasm download gets a per-call temp file and a rename into place, and is resolved once per test binary
  - tests/money_safety/src/wasms.rs: `icp_ledger_wasm()` is now a `OnceLock` around `resolve_icp_ledger_wasm()`, so the tests of one binary (cargo runs them on several threads; the fast gate uses `--test-threads=2`) wait for one fetch instead of each reaching `download` on a cold cache. `download(url)` curls into `unique_temp_path(cache_dir, "download")` = `download.<pid>.<nanos>.<seq>.tmp` (pid separates processes, an `AtomicU64` counter separates threads, nanos separates a restarted pid from a leftover), reads it and removes it; on a curl failure it removes its own temp file and panics with the same "Fetch it by hand into target/money-safety/ledger-canister.wasm.gz, or point $ICP_LEDGER_WASM at it" message. The hash-checked bytes go through `install_verified(dest, bytes)`: written to a unique sibling in the cache dir, then `rename`d over `ledger-canister.wasm.gz`, so a concurrent reader (another thread, another process, the settlement oracle's fallback to this cache) sees either no file or the whole file, never a partial write. The cache-hit path's "hash mismatch, remove and re-fetch" branch is kept; the comment says it can no longer be a half-written file.
  - tests/settlement/src/wasms.rs: same helper shape, same fix (`OnceLock`, `unique_temp_path`, `install_verified` into `target/settlement-oracle/ledger-canister.wasm.gz`, the "Fetch it by hand into target/settlement-oracle/..." message kept). Its fallback read of `target/money-safety/ledger-canister.wasm.gz` is unchanged and is now safe because that file is only ever renamed into place.
  - tests/no_peeking has no download helper (its only "download" is a canister snapshot download through PocketIC), so nothing to change there.
  - The old-release tree (`old-release-801aa79`) is not fetched by `download`; it is `git archive | tar -x` under its own `OnceLock`, once per binary, and the fast gate runs the money-safety binaries one after another, so it was not touched.

Canisters untouched: nothing under src/, Cargo.*, icp.yaml, .icp/, the frontend or scripts/ changed. No fund-moving code touched. `scripts/test-suites.list` unchanged (no new target).

